@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #ffffff
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam arrowColor #4b5563
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #4b5563
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #4b5563
hide footbox
title Market Desk | local shopper data

actor Shopper
participant "Market Desk\nweb layer" as Web
participant "Local services" as Service
database "H2" as DB

== Share a selected list ==

Shopper -> Web: Export selected list
Web -> Service: exportList(listId)
Service -> DB: Read list with items and retailer choices
Service --> Web: Versioned list records
Web --> Shopper: JSON download
Shopper -> Web: Upload file on receiving device
Web -> Service: importList(file)
Service -> Service: Validate all records
alt Valid file
  Service -> DB: Save named copy and inactive references as needed
  Web --> Shopper: Open the editable copy with local estimates
else Invalid file
  Web --> Shopper: Show import error
end

== Use a downloaded Cart offline ==

Shopper -> Web: Download selected Cart as HTML
Web -> Service: Read Cart, saved prices, retrieval time and budget
Service -> DB: Load the selected list and local settings
Service --> Web: Return the saved snapshot
Web --> Shopper: Download a self-contained HTML checklist
Shopper -> Shopper: Open file and update quantities,\nretailer, budget or Done status
note over Shopper: The file recalculates from its saved prices.\nChanges stay in the open file.

== View saved preferences and prices ==

Shopper -> Web: Choose language and contrast
Web -> Service: Save display preferences
Service -> DB: Update the local preference record
Shopper -> Web: Open price history for an exact pack
Web -> Service: Read the pack's retained observations
Service -> DB: Select records inside the 90-day window
Web --> Shopper: Show dates, retailers and Unknown gaps

== Export or reset personal data ==

Shopper -> Web: Export personal data
Web -> Web: Read the current session's chats
Web -> Service: Export saved personal records
Service -> DB: Read personal records
Web --> Shopper: Download JSON with personal records and session chats
Shopper -> Web: Confirm personal-data reset
Web -> Service: reset()
Service -> DB: Clear personal records and product-wide tracking in one transaction
alt Commit succeeds
  Service --> Web: Reset committed
  Web -> Web: Invalidate the current session
  Web --> Shopper: Show reset result
else Database failure
  Service --> Web: Reset rolled back
  Web --> Shopper: Show reset error
end
note over Service,DB: The accepted catalogue and import metadata stay available.
@enduml
